# mcpvuln writes `<target-basename>_security_report.md` into its current working
# directory in addition to the --json contract, so a scan run from the repository
# root drops one here. adapters/mcpvuln_adapter.py now runs the tool inside a
# temporary directory and tests/test_mcpvuln_adapter.py pins that, but this keeps
# a future adapter — or a hand-run of the tool — from committing them again.
# 78 had accumulated before the adapter was fixed.
*_security_report.md
